# .git-blame-ignore-revs
# List of commits that are irrelevant when traversing the blame history.
# GitHub automatically reads and interprets this file when present.
# Developers should run blame command as follows to exclude commits in this file:
# `git blame --ignore-revs-file .git-blame-ignore-revs <file-to-blame>`
# Or, to persist the exclusion, change the repo's configuration via:
# `git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs`
#
# More info at [^1] and [^2]:
# [^1] https://stackoverflow.com/questions/34957237/can-i-configure-git-blame-to-always-ignore-certain-commits-want-to-fix-git-blam
# [^2] https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/working-with-files/using-files/viewing-and-understanding-files#ignore-commits-in-the-blame-view

